Error [jet.ImmutableAssignment]: `hits` is module state, so a function can't change it directly
  --> tests/ui/module_write_from_fn_is_e0111.jet:9:5
    |
  9 |     hits += 1
    |     ^^^^
 Why: Every task sees module state, and two plain writes at once can lose one
 Fix: Keep it in a `shared` holder (`hits: shared Count{value: 0}`, written `hits.value += 1`) or mark it `#Persist`; code that needs a raw word writes it inside `#Unsafe("reason") { … }`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0111
